  "notes": "Verified modern scholarly article Work, originally published in Expedition 40(2), July 1998. It grounds the A02 route to exercise tablets, curricular extracts, lexical and literary training at Nippur and Ur while preserving tablet type, archaeological context, formation process, and survival bias. It is not the archaeological assemblage, a virtual Collection, an ancient Work, a physical tablet, a corpus release, or proof that every cited object was a school exercise. The Penn page labels the digitization a historical reference that may not reflect current museum views. Only Work identity and an unreviewed source-reported authorship claim are admitted; no article payload, Expression, Edition, Item, artifact membership, text, translation, semantic claim, graph relation, or canon state is created. A later A02 control-anchor planting must reuse this Work rather than duplicate it.",
